  "id": "ecological-validity",
  "term": "ecological validity",
  "definition": "Ecological validity is the extent to which an assessment reflects people’s behavior and experience in real-world settings. In this context, it refers to studying people in their natural environments rather than relying only on recall or artificial situations.",
